        "t0": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABHzAV3Q",
            "number": 1583,
            "title": "docs: fix file paths in static assets example",
            "body": "Resolves #1578\n\nThe \"Read files\" example mounts the handler at `/public/**`, but `serveStatic` passes the full request path as `id` (e.g. `/public/index.html`). So `join(\"public\", id)` looks for `public/public/index.html` and every request returns 404. The text also says to open `http://localhost:3000`, which isn't matched by `/public/**`.\n\nChanges:\n- Strip the `/public` prefix from `id` before joining it with the directory.\n- Point readers to `http://localhost:3000/public/`, after the full example.\n\nI checked both versions against h3 2.0.2 with a `public/index.html` file:\n\n| Path | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `/` | 404 | 404 (outside the mount, expected) |\n| `/public/` | 404 | 200 |\n| `/public/index.html` | 404 | 200 |\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated the static assets example to show creating `public/index.html` before opening `/public/` in a browser.\n  * Clarified that `/public` is removed from request paths before they’re used to read files or look up file metadata.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
